            <td data-label="Typical pay range">{row.range}</td>
            <td data-label="Context">{row.note}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div class="callout callout--teal">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      A banking sector career in India is a genuine skill-and-proof story, not a single-exam lottery. Entry
      pay differs by employer, but long-term pay differs more by specialization and consistency than by which
      logo is on your ID card. A credit officer or treasury specialist with 10 solid years of proof usually
      out-earns a generalist branch officer with the same tenure, in either PSU or private banking.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="checkpoint">The 4-Checkpoint Protocol before you commit</h2>
  <p>
    Before you spend a year or more preparing for one specific banking track, run yourself through the same
    four-part check that applies to any serious career decision: Biology, Context, Market, and Survival.
  </p>
  <div class="protocol-stack">
    {checkpointItems.map((item) => (
      <div class="protocol-row">
        <span class="protocol-num">{item.num}</span>
        <div class="protocol-body">
